record raw-autotune.observation.slice8-and-candidate-d-unblocked-20260828/1 : observation {
    title "Slice 8 GT pairs and Candidate D public-domain DCP unblocked the remaining heads"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Photographer brief docs/CAPTURE-AND-LICENCE-NEEDED.md is still the capture/licence note, but the two remaining heads it blocked are no longer waiting on data.

        Slice 8 (@raw-autotune.work.slice-8-local-tone-sky-ground-hdr-evaluation) used the backlit2 exposure pairs: hand-to-sky _DSC1345 vs _DSC1346 (−3.68 EV) and window _DSC1349 vs _DSC1348 (+3.35 EV). Scene-linear GT chroma shows reconstruction closer to the dark frame than reconstruction-disabled; hue is not a usable gate on handheld brackets. --local-tone and --hdr stay opt-in. Check local-tone-hdr-remain-colour-neutral is satisfied; the work is completed.

        Candidate D (@raw-autotune.work.calibrated-hue-sat-table-candidate-d): CamSDD has no colour chart. A ColorChecker is not available. The ART/RawTherapee SONY ILCE-7C.dcp is ProfileCopyright=public domain. --hue-sat-map ships default-off (src/huesatmap.rs, profiles/SONY_ILCE-7C.dcp). Remaining: held-out sky vs camera JPEG, no unattended enablement. Adobe DCP contents still must not be committed.

        Phase 4 remains closed (indoor WB and backlit fill both rejected). Working-tree dirt from the floor census, LinearRaw planner, indoor A/B and backlit2 A/B is still uncommitted; do not discard it. Slice-8/Candidate D code is in the same tree; keep commits split if committing.
        """
    observed_at git:00c933876fdd4fb9b7bec041cb78dc5474a02c18
    method command
}

