record raw-autotune.observation.spatial-highlight-false-colour-on-clipped-foliage/1 : observation {
    title "Spatial highlight estimators produce false colour on clipped indoor-outdoor foliage; per-pixel current matches the camera"
    state superseded
    statement """
        On indoor-outdoor frames with a large clipped exterior seen through an
        opening (raw/raw_backlit, 2-3 channels clipped over ~6% of pixels, max
        lift 4.8), both spatial highlight estimators paint the reconstructed
        foliage with large pink/magenta false-colour regions - harmonic (the
        default) and raw-pyramid alike - while --highlight-method current
        renders it nearly camera-like and --highlight-reconstruction 0 shows
        the raw magenta cast the solvers were meant to fix. Six-way crop grid
        incl. the camera JPEG:
        docs/evidence/phase4-backlit-20260827/ablation-grid.png. This is the
        purple-sky / unswept-spatial-floor family at first-order severity: on
        this batch it outweighs any backlit tone policy, and it is the defect
        a phase-4 render gate should address first (e.g. falling back to the
        per-pixel estimator, or bounding reconstruction chroma, on frames
        whose clipped region is large and chromatic).
        """
    observed_at git:c130e01d0b2eb60ea90e478b44b2d30e12716063
    method manual
    watches [ "src/raw_highlight*.rs", "src/color.rs" ]
}

record raw-autotune.observation.spatial-highlight-false-colour-on-clipped-foliage/2 : observation {
    title "Spatial-highlight false colour: root-caused to the heterogeneity guard's clipped-floor fallback; fixed in c09b7f9, residuals listed"
    state superseded
    statement """
        On indoor-outdoor frames with a large clipped exterior seen through an
        opening (raw/raw_backlit), both spatial highlight estimators painted
        the reconstructed area with large pink/magenta false-colour regions
        while --highlight-method current rendered it nearly camera-like.
        Root cause (found 2026-08-27, fixed in git c09b7f9): the joint chroma
        solve's region-global heterogeneity guard attenuated toward the
        clipped floor, whose chroma is the sensor's clipping order, not the
        scene — discarding a correct harmonic colour-line reconstruction
        (probed G 1.75 predicted vs 1.15 after the guard, ~1.71 true). The
        guard now falls back to neutral chroma at the harmonic luminance;
        the corpus-wide pink-patch population clears with coherent skies and
        sunsets byte-stable.

        Remaining follow-ups: (1) a weak residual pink patch top-right of
        _DSC1282 — likely cells with partial pairwise trust keeping a
        contaminated joint prediction; (2) the broad faint lavender cast on
        _DSC1288/1289, a separate cause untouched by this fix; (3) whether a
        local (windowed) coherence would beat the region-global scalar.
        """
    observed_at git:c09b7f95cee4a97af87a4428389819203ce2c749
    method manual
    watches [ "src/raw_highlight*.rs", "src/color.rs" ]
    supersedes [ @raw-autotune.observation.spatial-highlight-false-colour-on-clipped-foliage/1 ]
    verified_by [ @raw-autotune.evidence.harmonic-neutral-fallback-20260827 ]
}

record raw-autotune.observation.spatial-highlight-false-colour-on-clipped-foliage/3 : observation {
    title "Spatial-highlight false colour: root-caused to the heterogeneity guard's clipped-floor fallback; fixed in c09b7f9, residuals listed"
    state verified
    statement """
        On indoor-outdoor frames with a large clipped exterior seen through an
        opening (raw/raw_backlit), both spatial highlight estimators painted
        the reconstructed area with large pink/magenta false-colour regions
        while --highlight-method current rendered it nearly camera-like.
        Root cause (found 2026-08-27, fixed in git c09b7f9): the joint chroma
        solve's region-global heterogeneity guard attenuated toward the
        clipped floor, whose chroma is the sensor's clipping order, not the
        scene — discarding a correct harmonic colour-line reconstruction
        (probed G 1.75 predicted vs 1.15 after the guard, ~1.71 true). The
        guard now falls back to neutral chroma at the harmonic luminance;
        the corpus-wide pink-patch population clears with coherent skies and
        sunsets byte-stable.

        Follow-up outcomes (2026-08-27, git afb1cf0, archive-auto-v8):
            (1) the _DSC1282 residual patch is FIXED — the recomposition's base
            was still the raw clipped floor, reached in proportion to
            1 - luminance_support, and neutral_luminance could sit below a
            channel's white-balanced clip floor; the base now gets the same
            coherence blend as the target, anchored to the least-commitment
            clip_neutral (see
            @raw-autotune.evidence.harmonic-base-neutralization-20260827).
            (2) the broad faint lavender cast on _DSC1288/1289 is ACQUITTED as
            a solver defect: the unclipped sky genuinely measures blue-violet
            (CFA B/R 1.43 under as-shot WB) and the divergence from the camera
            is its stronger highlight-to-white shoulder plus our 0.25-0.57 EV
            darker sky — a look decision, with a clip-gated white-path
            candidate held unmerged on fix/lavender-cast (see
            @raw-autotune.evidence.lavender-cast-is-faithful-rendering-20260827);
            _DSC1249/1250/1253/1258 belong to this population. The darker-sky
            half connects to
            @raw-autotune.work.midtone-shadow-contrast-versus-reference-renderers.
            (3) the local-windowed coherence idea is moot for this defect —
            base neutralization removed the failure mode it targeted.
        """
    observed_at git:afb1cf091b6278882b5d06b0a4ab8ff0e666ac42
    method manual
    watches [ "src/raw_highlight*.rs", "src/color.rs" ]
    supersedes [ @raw-autotune.observation.spatial-highlight-false-colour-on-clipped-foliage/2 ]
    verified_by [ @raw-autotune.evidence.harmonic-neutral-fallback-20260827 ]
}
